{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":634543,"ns":0,"title":"Bendixson–Dulac theorem","extract":"In mathematics, the Bendixson–Dulac theorem is a theorem in dynamical systems that exclude the existence of periodic orbits of two-dimensional flows. Here a flow can be visualized as the surface of a pond.","description":"Mathematical theory on dynamical systems","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}